        "markdown": "# PHILIP MORRIS LIMITED\n\nA.C.N. 004 694 428\n\nhandwritten note: to Han Kimber Lutterio\n\n## Facsimile Message\n\n**TO:** DISTRIBUTION\n**FROM:** GREG FOWLER\n**DATE:** SEPTEMBER 17, 1993.\n**REF:** A:BRCPRO.GLF3 PAGE 1 OF 12\n**SUBJECT:** <u>BURSWOOD RESORT CASINO PROSECUTION</u>\n\nI am pleased to report that the Western Australian court dismissed the Health Department's ETS-based claims against Burswood Casino.\n\nAttached is the TIA's Press Release and the court's Reasons for Decision. The court stated its conclusion as follows:\n\n> Whilst ETS is annoying and of discomfort to non smokers it has not been proved at the required standard, or at all, in this prosecution, that it is a risk to the health of the employees at the Casino.\n\nAt pages 8-9 of the Reasons, the Court considered but rejected the EPA Risk Assessment's \"conclusion\" on ETS and respiratory illness.\n\nRegards,\n\nsignature: Akto\n\nfor <u>GREGORY L. FOWLER</u>\n\n<u>Distribution:</u> David Davies\nJudy Hargrave\nPeter Hobday\nTim Lindon\nBob Northrip\nSteve Parrish\nLee Pollak\nDavid Schechter\nChuck Wall",
